# reading 2 of locke-treatise-3.md by claude-opus-5-5
atom	distinct_persons	in a commonwealth the members are distinct persons in reference to one another
atom	governed_by_laws	the members, as distinct persons, are governed by the laws of the society
atom	one_body	in reference to the rest of mankind, the members of a commonwealth make one body
atom	state_of_nature	that body is still in the state of nature with the rest of mankind, as every member of it before was
atom	natural_power	there is another power in every commonwealth which one may call natural
atom	answers_natural_power	that power answers to the power every man naturally had before he entered into society
atom	public_manages	controversies between any man of the society and those out of it are managed by the public
atom	injury_engages_whole	an injury done to a member of their body engages the whole in the reparation of it
